        {
          "id": 1156431840,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Looking closer at [the root `CMakeLists.txt`](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/a1c55f2356c90dbd60861e33270f875b24734346/CMakeLists.txt#L1927-1962) shows it already has a `CUSTOM_TSHARK_TAP_SRC` variable, but this does not get populated anywhere. This would need to be added to the root `CMakeListsCustom.txt.example`.\n\n`epan/dissectors/CMakeLists.txt` does *not* handle any taps, so the MR upon which we are discussing this would not be affected even if it were not merged.\n\nEditorial: it seems a bit strange to me that all the taps of interest are in `ui/cli/` but are listed in the root `CMakeLists.txt` file. It feels like there should be a `ui/cli/CMakeLists.txt` and accompanying example custom file for these taps. I need to learn more about CMake before deciding if this either possible or desirable.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6020526,
            "username": "boolean263",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "David Perry",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6020526/avatar.png?v=1789780429",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/boolean263"
